{{!-- The plan cards, priced from the publication's live Tiers.

	{{> "membership/tiers"}}                     A1's, under the centred statement
	{{> "membership/tiers" padding="pt-14"}}     A2's, under the ruled-off split hero

	padding   the section's top padding

STALE PRICES ARE THE WORST FAILURE MODE IN THIS THEME, so nothing here is written down. Names,
descriptions, benefits and both prices come from `{{#get "tiers"}}`, and every amount goes through
`{{price}}` — `monthly_price` is an integer in the currency's smallest unit (800, not 8), and
printing it raw would advertise a $800 membership.

Both price sets are in the markup and Alpine swaps them, exactly as the design source does: the
page stays static, and a reader with no JavaScript sees the monthly prices rather than an empty
card. The Handlebars runs once, at render; `x-text` only chooses between two strings it already
holds.

WHAT THE DESIGN CLAIMS AND GHOST CANNOT. The source's yearly note reads "Two months free · billed
annually" and its yearly pill reads "−17%". Both are arithmetic over two prices, Handlebars has
none, and a theme that hardcoded either would print a discount that a publication with different
prices does not offer. The note reads "Billed annually" and the pill carries no percentage.
Recorded as a Concession in DECISIONS.md.

`href` is a Portal deep link and works with JavaScript off only as far as Portal is loaded;
`data-portal` is the attribute Portal binds to. The pair is what makes the button open the real
signup for that tier and cadence rather than a page the theme invented.

The free tier prints the theme's own word rather than a formatted zero: a free tier carries no
currency in Ghost, and `{{price 0}}` with no currency returns a bare `0`. --}}
{{#if @site.members_enabled}}
	<section
		id="tiers"
		aria-labelledby="tiers-h"
		class="container {{#if padding}}{{padding}}{{/if}}"
		x-data="{ yearly: false }">
		<h2
			id="tiers-h"
			class="sr-only">{{t "Plans"}}</h2>

		{{!-- THE SWITCH FOLLOWS THE TIERS, NOT THE STRIPE FLAG. `@site.paid_members_enabled` is false
		until Stripe is connected, and a publication that has written its plans but not yet plugged
		in payments would lose the control that reveals its own yearly prices — measured on this
		install, where three tiers exist and the flag is false. The condition that matters is
		whether there is a second price to switch to, which is exactly "does a paid tier exist". --}}
		{{#get "tiers" filter="type:paid" limit="1" as |paid|}}
			{{#if paid}}
				<div class="mb-9 flex justify-center">
					<div
						role="group"
						aria-label="{{t "Billing period"}}"
						class="border-border bg-surface-2 rounded-pill flex gap-0.5 border p-[3px]">
						<button
							type="button"
							x-on:click="yearly = false"
							x-bind:aria-pressed="(!yearly).toString()"
							x-bind:class="yearly ? 'bg-transparent text-muted' : 'bg-text text-surface'"
							class="rounded-pill font-ui cursor-pointer border-0 px-5 py-[9px] text-[13px] font-semibold">{{t "Monthly"}}</button>
						<button
							type="button"
							x-on:click="yearly = true"
							x-bind:aria-pressed="yearly.toString()"
							x-bind:class="yearly ? 'bg-text text-surface' : 'bg-transparent text-muted'"
							class="rounded-pill font-ui cursor-pointer border-0 px-5 py-[9px] text-[13px] font-semibold">{{t "Yearly"}}</button>
					</div>
				</div>
			{{/if}}
		{{/get}}

		{{#get "tiers" include="monthly_price,yearly_price,benefits" limit="100" as |tiers|}}
			{{#if tiers}}
				<div class="grid grid-cols-[repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(280px,100%),1fr))] items-stretch gap-6">
					{{#foreach tiers}}
						{{#match type "free"}}
							<article class="border-border bg-surface flex flex-col rounded-md border p-8">
								<div class="flex items-center gap-2.5">
									<h3 class="font-display tracking-heading text-[22px] font-medium">{{name}}</h3>
								</div>

								<p class="mt-5 flex items-baseline gap-2">
									<span class="font-display tracking-display text-[46px] leading-none font-medium">{{t "Free"}}</span>
									<span class="font-meta text-meta tracking-meta text-muted uppercase">{{t "forever"}}</span>
								</p>

								<p class="text-muted mt-2.5 font-mono text-[11.5px]">{{t "No card required"}}</p>

								{{#if description}}
									<p class="text-small text-muted mt-[18px] leading-[1.6]">{{description}}</p>
								{{/if}}

								<ul class="mt-[22px] mb-auto flex list-none flex-col gap-[11px] p-0">
									{{#foreach benefits}}
										<li class="flex items-start gap-[11px]">
											<span
												aria-hidden="true"
												class="text-accent flex-none font-mono text-xs leading-[1.6]">&check;</span>
											<span class="text-small leading-[1.6]">{{this}}</span>
										</li>
									{{/foreach}}
								</ul>

								<a
									href="#/portal/signup/free"
									data-portal="signup/free"
									class="btn border-text text-text hover:bg-text hover:text-surface font-ui mt-[26px] block rounded-sm border px-[22px] py-[13px] text-center text-[15px] font-semibold no-underline">{{t "Join free"}}</a>
							</article>
						{{else}}
							<article
								class="flex flex-col rounded-md border p-8 {{#match name @custom.featured_tier}}border-accent-border bg-accent-soft{{else}}border-border bg-surface{{/match}}">
								<div class="flex items-center gap-2.5">
									<h3 class="font-display tracking-heading text-[22px] font-medium">{{name}}</h3>

									{{#match name @custom.featured_tier}}
										<span
											class="rounded-pill bg-accent text-on-accent px-[9px] py-[3px] font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[0.08em] uppercase">{{t "Most popular"}}</span>
									{{/match}}
								</div>

								<p class="mt-5 flex items-baseline gap-2">
									<span
										class="font-display tracking-display text-[46px] leading-none font-medium"
										x-text="yearly ? '{{price yearly_price currency=currency}}' : '{{price monthly_price currency=currency}}'">{{price monthly_price currency=currency}}</span>
									<span
										class="font-meta text-meta tracking-meta text-muted uppercase"
										x-text="yearly ? '{{t "per year"}}' : '{{t "per month"}}'">{{t "per month"}}</span>
								</p>

								<p
									class="text-muted mt-2.5 font-mono text-[11.5px]"
									x-text="yearly ? '{{t "Billed annually"}}' : '{{t "Or {price} per year" price=(price yearly_price currency=currency)}}'">{{t "Or {price} per year" price=(price yearly_price currency=currency)}}</p>

								{{#if description}}
									<p class="text-small text-muted mt-[18px] leading-[1.6]">{{description}}</p>
								{{/if}}

								<ul class="mt-[22px] mb-auto flex list-none flex-col gap-[11px] p-0">
									{{#foreach benefits}}
										<li class="flex items-start gap-[11px]">
											<span
												aria-hidden="true"
												class="text-accent flex-none font-mono text-xs leading-[1.6]">&check;</span>
											<span class="text-small leading-[1.6]">{{this}}</span>
										</li>
									{{/foreach}}
								</ul>

								<a
									href="#/portal/signup/{{id}}/monthly"
									data-portal="signup/{{id}}/monthly"
									x-bind:href="yearly ? '#/portal/signup/{{id}}/yearly' : '#/portal/signup/{{id}}/monthly'"
									x-bind:data-portal="yearly ? 'signup/{{id}}/yearly' : 'signup/{{id}}/monthly'"
									class="btn font-ui mt-[26px] block rounded-sm border px-[22px] py-[13px] text-center text-[15px] font-semibold no-underline {{#match name @custom.featured_tier}}btn-primary{{else}}border-text text-text hover:bg-text hover:text-surface{{/match}}"
									x-text="yearly ? '{{t "Choose {tier} — {price}/year" tier=name price=(price yearly_price currency=currency)}}' : '{{t "Choose {tier} — {price}/month" tier=name price=(price monthly_price currency=currency)}}'">{{t "Choose {tier} — {price}/month" tier=name price=(price monthly_price currency=currency)}}</a>
							</article>
						{{/match}}
					{{/foreach}}
				</div>
			{{/if}}
		{{/get}}
	</section>
{{/if}}
